WEBVTT

00:14.650 --> 00:15.770
What's the matter?

00:15.770 --> 00:18.450
The air is shaking slightly.

00:23.090 --> 00:25.540
We should be right below the marketplace...

00:25.960 --> 00:27.290
Could that be the reason?

00:27.290 --> 00:30.260
No, I hear it.

00:31.300 --> 00:32.550
It sounds like...

00:33.050 --> 00:34.050
water?

00:35.580 --> 00:38.510
The sound of splashing water...

00:41.770 --> 00:42.790
Pursuers?!

00:42.790 --> 00:43.430
Which way?

00:44.770 --> 00:45.520
Ahead of us!

00:46.000 --> 00:47.530
This is bad! We must turn back!

00:53.650 --> 00:55.450
Are we on a singular path?

00:55.850 --> 00:58.410
The path we were following was!

00:58.410 --> 01:00.120
But it's a labyrinth behind us!

01:00.530 --> 01:04.580
Even I am not confident 
of navigating my way through here.

01:07.830 --> 01:08.970
What's the matter?

01:08.970 --> 01:10.650
They will catch up to us even if we run.

01:11.100 --> 01:13.660
They have released hounds.

01:15.990 --> 01:18.430
They sound quite dim-witted.

01:18.730 --> 01:21.510
Well, cover your ears.

01:36.820 --> 01:37.710
What?

01:50.250 --> 01:53.000
I wish I could eat some apples...

01:54.730 --> 01:56.630
You can eat your fill later.

01:58.470 --> 02:02.690
Spice and Wolf

02:02.690 --> 02:03.810
Spice and Wolf

02:03.810 --> 02:09.150
Spice and Wolf

03:30.230 --> 03:33.070
I wonder how they found out where we were?

03:31.350 --> 03:36.360
<b>Episode 6
Merchant and Unreasonable God</b>

03:33.070 --> 03:36.860
They probably happened to find us after 
looking through various underground passages.

03:36.860 --> 03:38.300
You think so?

03:38.300 --> 03:42.910
If they knew exactly where we were, they 
would have sandwiched us from both sides.

03:45.550 --> 03:47.790
The Milone Trading Company 
sold us your information!

03:47.790 --> 03:49.540
There's no point in running!

03:51.120 --> 03:53.750
He says we have been sold off...

03:54.490 --> 03:56.810
It must have been a pretty penny.

03:56.810 --> 04:00.120
After all, they could have crushed the Milone 
Trading Company as long as they had you.

04:00.120 --> 04:03.470
I see. Then, the price 
must have been exorbitant.

04:03.470 --> 04:05.850
They're just bluffing and trying their luck.

04:06.390 --> 04:07.140
Let's go.

04:09.810 --> 04:10.810
Hold on.

04:13.150 --> 04:14.290
I found them!

04:16.690 --> 04:18.480
There they are! Don't let them escape!

04:18.480 --> 04:21.210
Keep chasing them! I'll go around from behind!

04:21.210 --> 04:22.470
Got it!

04:22.470 --> 04:24.250
I heard footsteps in that direction!

04:24.250 --> 04:25.220
Corner them!

04:25.220 --> 04:26.930
They haven't come this way yet!

04:26.930 --> 04:28.580
Cut off all their paths!

04:29.910 --> 04:31.500
Do you know where you're going?

04:31.500 --> 04:33.950
Yeah, we'll be fine. Go left next!

04:46.850 --> 04:47.890
Let's hurry!

04:56.290 --> 04:57.310
Lawrence!

04:57.790 --> 05:01.010
God, please forgive my sins.

05:07.870 --> 05:11.870
Before asking forgiveness for your sins, 
how about repenting your current way of life?

05:19.810 --> 05:20.880
Lawrence?

05:21.510 --> 05:24.260
It's fine. I know where we're going.

05:29.170 --> 05:31.040
Shit! Where'd they go?!

05:29.900 --> 05:31.040
Hey! Over here!

05:31.040 --> 05:32.930
He's completely out.

05:32.930 --> 05:34.110
After them!

05:36.740 --> 05:40.230
Lawrence! Are you all right?

05:40.790 --> 05:41.910
Lawrence!

05:44.020 --> 05:45.190
Thank goodness...

05:45.570 --> 05:48.550
You would not move, no matter 
how many times I called you.

05:49.860 --> 05:53.060
It's fine. I was just a bit sleepy.

05:53.370 --> 05:56.290
Hang in there. We are almost there.

05:56.290 --> 05:57.600
What are you talking about?

05:57.600 --> 05:59.120
Do you not hear me?

05:59.120 --> 06:03.800
I said, "I smell light. There must be 
a place that leads to the surface."

06:03.800 --> 06:06.470
Y-Yeah, you did...

06:07.990 --> 06:08.720
What's this?

06:08.720 --> 06:12.050
You failed to notice that as well?!

06:15.370 --> 06:16.560
Just a bit further.

06:17.010 --> 06:18.430
It's just a bit further.

06:21.260 --> 06:25.400
No, I noticed. I'm fine.

06:32.210 --> 06:33.170
This way.

06:37.090 --> 06:39.730
If we follow that path 
and turn left at the end of it,

06:39.730 --> 06:41.790
we should be able to escape to the surface.

06:55.220 --> 06:56.770
Impossible...

06:57.260 --> 06:59.230
An old well.

06:59.850 --> 07:03.290
I am sorry. I did not think 
this would happen...

07:03.290 --> 07:04.220
There they are!

07:07.990 --> 07:09.210
Stand back.

07:10.450 --> 07:11.520
No way...

07:11.520 --> 07:12.780
It will be impossible for you.

07:12.780 --> 07:13.660
Don't worry,

07:16.130 --> 07:17.830
I can handle a few more rounds.

07:18.180 --> 07:21.210
Lies! I do not even need my ears 
to tell you that you are lying!

07:22.110 --> 07:23.060
Hold on.

07:26.920 --> 07:30.970
The informant described 
your appearance, so I thought...

07:31.610 --> 07:34.790
I can't believe it was really you, Lawrence.

07:35.290 --> 07:36.970
I was surprised, too.

07:37.250 --> 07:40.930
I never took you for a guy who'd 
get involved in a big deal like this.

07:40.930 --> 07:43.450
You've really grown, Yarei.

07:45.890 --> 07:49.440
Count Erhendott is the one 
behind Medio Trading...

07:50.050 --> 07:51.530
A large wheat producing land

07:51.530 --> 07:55.280
can receive payment in any kind of 
silver coin they like in their dealings.

07:55.560 --> 08:00.610
On top of that, tariff exemptions 
on wheat would be a great blessing

08:00.610 --> 08:03.500
for the count, Medio Trading, 
and the villagers...

08:03.930 --> 08:07.170
You're acquainted with all 
the merchants that come to trade,

08:07.170 --> 08:09.300
and the chief leaves 
all the business dealings to you.

08:09.640 --> 08:14.220
And, the trade of wheat is most abundant 
right after the harvest festival.

08:14.220 --> 08:17.220
Well, we can catch up later.

08:17.220 --> 08:18.010
There's currently no time.

08:18.010 --> 08:20.150
How cold, Yarei.

08:20.150 --> 08:22.770
You went through all the trouble of coming here

08:22.770 --> 08:24.690
to see the wolf you 
didn't believe in, didn't you?

08:24.690 --> 08:27.400
I can't believe you're her companion.

08:27.720 --> 08:34.090
The incarnation of a wolf that lives in 
our wheat and controls our harvests at will.

08:34.850 --> 08:36.780
Hand her over.

08:36.780 --> 08:41.160
We will hand her over to the church 
and say good-bye to the old era.

08:41.500 --> 08:45.420
We'll be able to crush 
Milone Trading if we hand her over.

08:47.370 --> 08:49.930
On top of that, 
if we can remove the tariffs on wheat,

08:49.930 --> 08:53.010
our village will gain 
an enormous amount of profit.

08:53.010 --> 08:55.380
The villagers will all become prosperous.

08:56.020 --> 08:57.010
Lawrence...

08:57.010 --> 09:00.510
The same goes for the merchants 
that buy our wheat.

09:00.820 --> 09:05.410
The villagers are all grateful 
that you bought our wheat

09:05.410 --> 09:07.900
when we were suffering under heavy taxation.

09:07.900 --> 09:12.400
It'll be easy for you to obtain 
priority in buying our wheat.

09:12.740 --> 09:15.950
We've been friends for a long time, haven't we?

09:15.950 --> 09:19.490
You'll be able to obtain 
the store of your dreams.

09:19.780 --> 09:24.000
Then, we'll be able to get involved 
in even bigger businesses.

09:24.320 --> 09:26.780
I learned how to do business from you.

09:26.780 --> 09:30.310
This time, I want to help 
you succeed in your business.

09:30.980 --> 09:32.590
Come on, Lawrence.

09:32.590 --> 09:36.180
As a merchant, you can calculate 
profit and loss, can't you?

09:39.210 --> 09:41.430
Of course I can.

09:43.580 --> 09:44.650
Lawrence!

09:44.650 --> 09:45.500
However...

09:45.930 --> 09:50.210
First and foremost, a good merchant 
must honor their contracts.

09:50.940 --> 09:52.740
As fate would have it,

09:52.740 --> 09:56.700
I ended up picking up a strange girl 
that wants to go back home to the north.

09:57.060 --> 10:01.070
I already promised her that I would 
keep her company during her journey.

10:01.550 --> 10:04.490
I can't go against my contractual obligations.

10:08.150 --> 10:11.750
Then, all I can do is fulfill 
my own contractual obligations.

10:11.750 --> 10:16.540
How unfortunate. Looks like 
our relationship ends here, Lawrence.

10:16.540 --> 10:19.260
Traveling merchants 
are familiar with farewells.

10:21.470 --> 10:23.270
You can kill the man.

10:23.740 --> 10:25.890
Make sure to capture the woman alive.

10:37.730 --> 10:38.900
Holo?!

10:42.160 --> 10:43.300
The dagger...

10:45.110 --> 10:45.910
Enough!

10:47.460 --> 10:51.110
It may hurt a bit, but you must endure.

11:02.490 --> 11:03.820
She's sucking his blood!

11:13.490 --> 11:14.750
Don't flinch!

11:14.750 --> 11:17.610
She's merely a woman possessed by the devil!

11:23.450 --> 11:26.820
Do not look any longer.

13:13.020 --> 13:16.500
Th-The gods are always the same.

13:16.500 --> 13:19.730
They're always... always so unfair...

13:22.460 --> 13:23.530
Holo...

13:28.910 --> 13:30.700
Stop, Holo!

14:05.450 --> 14:06.370
Wait...

14:07.430 --> 14:08.240
Holo!

14:15.610 --> 14:18.790
How much do you think 
the clothes you tore up cost?!

14:18.790 --> 14:21.710
Whether you're a god or not, 
I'll have you compensate me!

14:21.710 --> 14:25.960
You only earned 70 silver coins! 
That's not enough at all!

14:25.960 --> 14:29.850
How many years do you think it took me 
to earn enough money for them?!

14:32.140 --> 14:33.890
I'll chase after you!

14:33.890 --> 14:37.390
I'll chase after you all the way 
to the forests of the north!

14:45.420 --> 14:46.420
Holo!

14:50.610 --> 14:51.820
Ho... lo...

15:09.820 --> 15:11.440
Have you awoken?

15:12.200 --> 15:14.490
Is your wound doing all right?

15:14.490 --> 15:16.720
Yes, thanks to you.

15:16.720 --> 15:22.060
I apologize for causing you so much trouble 
due to our poor execution of matters.

15:22.060 --> 15:26.820
No, this all happened because of my companion.

15:29.500 --> 15:32.320
Luckily, the Church was unable to find her.

15:32.320 --> 15:36.300
It's fortunate that everything happened 
in the underground passages.

15:36.300 --> 15:39.790
If the public saw her form,

15:39.790 --> 15:43.220
our headquarters and branches 
may have all been burnt to the ground.

15:43.220 --> 15:44.420
You saw her true form?!

15:44.810 --> 15:45.790
Yes.

15:46.570 --> 15:49.130
I received a report from my subordinates.

15:49.440 --> 15:53.640
The report stated there was a giant wolf 
protecting you that wouldn't move.

15:53.640 --> 15:59.620
I came to see the situation in person 
and saw your companion there.

16:01.880 --> 16:02.940
She was protecting me?!

16:03.730 --> 16:05.690
So, where is Holo now?!

16:06.430 --> 16:09.940
Well, after we brought you here...

16:14.650 --> 16:17.470
She left without telling us her destination.

16:20.170 --> 16:21.100
When?

16:21.100 --> 16:23.460
It has been an entire day since then...

16:24.020 --> 16:25.490
I see.

16:31.510 --> 16:32.340
So...

16:32.740 --> 16:34.810
Did the deal go well?

16:34.810 --> 16:39.100
Yes. We were able to obtain 
the privilege that Medio Trading

16:39.100 --> 16:41.220
desired most from the royal family.

16:41.220 --> 16:45.100
It is unlikely that your companion 
will be reported to the Church.

16:45.100 --> 16:46.600
That's good to hear.

16:46.600 --> 16:52.250
We were able to collect 307,212 silver coins.

16:52.250 --> 16:56.410
It seems His Majesty plans to 
devalue the coins quite drastically.

16:56.410 --> 16:59.480
He agreed to pay us immediately 
in another currency worth

16:59.480 --> 17:01.410
350,000 silver coins at the time of delivery.

17:01.410 --> 17:03.120
350,000 coins?!

17:03.120 --> 17:09.500
According to our contract, 
you receive fifty percent of our profits.

17:09.970 --> 17:12.000
Am I correct?

17:12.000 --> 17:12.800
Yes...

17:13.120 --> 17:14.500
Please confirm our calculations.

17:14.950 --> 17:15.630
Yes.

17:17.070 --> 17:17.930
This is...

17:17.930 --> 17:22.640
120 silver coins. 
That is fifty percent of our profit.

17:23.050 --> 17:25.730
Is that... all?

17:25.730 --> 17:28.780
The delivery costs of the coins we collected...

17:28.780 --> 17:30.980
As well as the tariffs that come with it...

17:30.980 --> 17:35.280
Also, the handling fees 
for the contract itself...

17:36.310 --> 17:38.570
This is a ridiculous amount of contract fees...

17:38.570 --> 17:42.190
The royal family's official merchants 
probably gave him the idea.

17:42.190 --> 17:44.080
Since he was trading off privileges,

17:44.370 --> 17:48.550
he wanted to recoup as much 
of his financial losses as possible.

17:49.210 --> 17:52.050
Our total profits were 2,400 silver coins.

17:52.320 --> 17:55.570
It was an unimaginably disappointing result.

17:55.570 --> 17:59.300
Unexpected things always happen in business...

17:59.700 --> 18:00.800
However...

18:01.160 --> 18:05.430
Unexpected things can 
also happen in a good way.

18:07.050 --> 18:08.120
Take a look at this.

18:11.160 --> 18:11.940
This is...

18:11.940 --> 18:16.070
It seems Medio Trading 
was quite desperate for this privilege.

18:16.070 --> 18:17.280
On top of that,

18:17.280 --> 18:21.160
they were collecting silver coins even though 
they knew the coins' value would drop.

18:21.160 --> 18:24.120
That is the same as going into debt.

18:24.620 --> 18:29.790
They must have been determined 
to make sure their business turned a profit.

18:30.080 --> 18:33.340
They offered an amount 
we could accept on the spot.

18:33.820 --> 18:36.760
1,000 silver coins... Are you sure?

18:36.760 --> 18:39.320
Yes, it was a great deal for us.

18:39.320 --> 18:41.740
Would you like the payment in silver coins?

18:41.740 --> 18:45.720
If you like, I can arrange 
an equivalent value in product instead.

18:48.540 --> 18:49.690
Pepper.

18:50.170 --> 18:51.810
Do you have pepper?

18:51.810 --> 18:53.650
It's light and doesn't take up much space.

18:53.930 --> 18:55.370
Pepper?

18:55.370 --> 18:59.570
The price of pepper will rise as winter 
arrives and people cook more meat.

19:01.230 --> 19:02.370
What's the matter?

19:02.370 --> 19:04.340
My apologies.

19:04.340 --> 19:07.570
I just remembered a play I read recently.

19:07.570 --> 19:08.540
Play?

19:09.220 --> 19:10.170
Yes.

19:10.940 --> 19:13.010
It's a religious play that the Church uses

19:13.010 --> 19:16.580
to preach about moderation 
to trading companies.

19:16.580 --> 19:20.880
A devil appears before an extremely 
rich merchant and says to him,

19:21.260 --> 19:26.390
"Bring me the most delicious human 
in the land, or I will eat you instead."

19:26.730 --> 19:28.780
Fearing for his life,

19:28.780 --> 19:32.660
he brings a young maidservant 
and fat servant before the devil,

19:32.660 --> 19:35.730
but the devil shakes his head.

19:35.730 --> 19:39.050
He searches all over town 
for a delicious human.

19:39.050 --> 19:42.920
Finally, he finds a boy 
who smells of honey and milk.

19:42.920 --> 19:48.040
He offers that boy immediately to 
the devil, but the boy says to the devil,

19:48.530 --> 19:51.160
"The most delicious human 
is before your very eyes."

19:51.610 --> 20:00.740
"This man before you seasons his fat-laden 
soul abundantly with spices day after day."

20:02.300 --> 20:04.390
Sorry, I could not help it.

20:05.380 --> 20:10.220
I imagined you earning money 
using pepper, Mr. Lawrence.

20:11.110 --> 20:14.130
I would love to be laden 
with spices as soon as possible.

20:14.130 --> 20:15.850
I look forward to it.

20:15.850 --> 20:19.400
After all, we always wish 
to build a good relationship

20:19.400 --> 20:22.340
with merchants as talented as yourself.

20:24.490 --> 20:25.950
Thank you very much.

20:26.260 --> 20:28.930
I will prepare your pepper.

20:28.930 --> 20:31.910
There is still work to be done,
so I will take my leave.

20:35.810 --> 20:39.670
Mr. Lawrence, we received 
an invoice with your name on it.

20:43.070 --> 20:47.720
140 silver coins? I don't remember 
purchasing these products...

20:56.370 --> 20:57.770
Where is your loading area?

20:57.770 --> 21:00.480
Oh, well, it's right down 
that hallway and to the left...

21:00.480 --> 21:01.350
Thanks!

21:05.130 --> 21:06.550
A woman's robe,

21:07.280 --> 21:08.530
silk sash,

21:09.250 --> 21:10.740
traveling shoes,

21:11.080 --> 21:12.650
and a tortoiseshell comb!

21:18.420 --> 21:19.850
Excuse me! Please let me through!

21:21.450 --> 21:22.260
And,

21:22.590 --> 21:23.980
an enormous number of apples!

21:22.920 --> 21:25.920
That'll be 40 silver coins.

21:25.920 --> 21:26.620
Holo!

21:36.940 --> 21:40.570
I cannot have you coming all the way 
to the forests of the north to collect a debt.

21:56.330 --> 21:59.330
I will return home after I have repaid you.

22:00.590 --> 22:01.840
Of course.

22:08.140 --> 22:10.910
Spice and Wolf, is it?

23:45.020 --> 23:50.030
Episode 7

23:45.020 --> 23:50.030
Scale of God and Sorcerer of the Grasslands

23:45.650 --> 23:49.710
Next Episode: Scale of God 
and Sorcerer of the Grasslands
